{title: 314 - Just as I Am}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #314 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 314}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Just as I am, with[A]out [A7]one [D]plea,
[D]But [A]that [D]Thy [A7]blood was [G]shed [D]for me,
[D]And that Thou bidst me [G]come to Thee,
[G]O [D]Lamb of God, I [A]come, I [D]come.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Just [A]as I [A7]am, and [D]waiting not
[D]to [A]rid [D]my soul [A7]of [G]one [D]dark blot,
[D]to thee whose blood [G]can cleanse each spot,
[G]O Lamb [D]of God, [A]I come, [D]I come.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Just [A]as I [A7]am, though [D]tossed about
[D]with [A]many [D]a [A7]conflict, [G]many [D]a doubt,
[D]fightings and [G]fears within, without,
[G]O Lamb [D]of God, [A]I come, [D]I come.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Just [A]as I [A7]am, poor, [D]wretched, blind;
[D]sight, [A]riches, [D]healing [A7]of [G]the [D]mind,
[D]yea, all I need [G]in thee to find,
[G]O Lamb [D]of God, [A]I come, [D]I come.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]Just [A]as I [A7]am, thou [D]wilt receive,
[D][A]wilt [D]welcome, [A7]pardon, [G]cleanse, [D]relieve;
[D]because thy [G]promise I believe,
[G]O Lamb [D]of God, [A]I come, [D]I come.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[D]Just as [A]I am, [A7]thy love [D]I own
[D][A]hath [D]broken [A7]every [G]barrier [D]down;
[D]now, to be [G]thine, and thine alone,
[G]O Lamb [D]of God, [A]I come, [D]I come.
{end_of_verse}
